# Review gate (06 §7, 07 Phase 0): guarded paths require human review before merge.
# Replace @your-org/* with the real reviewing teams when forking this GitOps repo.
# CODEOWNERS is necessary but not sufficient — enable a branch-protection ruleset that REQUIRES
# code-owner review + status checks on these paths (see .github/branch-protection.md).

# Provisioning (cloud/cluster resources authored as KCC YAML or Terraform HCL)
/clusters/*/provisioning/         @your-org/platform-admins

# Tenant namespace config: RBAC, NetworkPolicy, ResourceQuota, workloads. Under Config Sync
# (README, "Reconciler") an object's namespace comes from its metadata, not this directory, so
# reject a RootSync or RepoSync here: it gets a reconciler of its own. Nothing enforces this yet (#3163).
/clusters/*/namespaces/           @your-org/cluster-admins

# Config Sync's own namespace: a RootSync or RepoSync here gets a reconciler of its own (a
# RootSync's is cluster-admin unless spec.override.roleRefs narrows it) syncing a source outside this repository, so it carries the
# same review as provisioning/. Last match wins, so this line must stay below the one above.
/clusters/*/namespaces/config-management-system/  @your-org/platform-admins

# Agent CRs + per-agent identity manifests (KSA/RBAC/WI)
/clusters/*/agents/               @your-org/platform-admins
/fleet/                           @your-org/platform-admins

# Admission policies (the security backstop itself)
/policy/                          @your-org/security

# Declared intent: a knowledge/ note can move an audit posture off the ledger
# (README, "Declared intent"), so it carries the same review as provisioning/
/knowledge/                       @your-org/platform-admins

# Intent bounds: .kube-agents/intent.yaml decides which paths' notes the audit reads, and
# removing it opens the whole repository to them, so it carries the same review as knowledge/
/.kube-agents/                    @your-org/platform-admins
